# Rung 5a: the user's trigger. Host A. Not config-aware.
#
# Three requests to a service that is ALREADY RUNNING. That is the whole of the 5a
# model in two lines of shell: the caller does not create the agent, does not choose its
# image, does not pick its scope and cannot end it. It addresses a mailbox and something
# on the other side handles it.
#
# The delegation is the goal's root capability, narrowed by dropping read_wiki on the way
# past. The reader service never sees the goal record; it sees what this hop handed it,
# and host A's capability authority checked that against what this hop actually holds
# before the message was queued.
#
# Three requests rather than one, because a standing service that handles exactly one
# message is a task with extra steps. The recycle policy's residual window is measured in
# exchanges, so there have to be several.

send-agent --tag req1 --delegate-file /scratch/delegate.json reader investigate incident 4471
send-agent --tag req2 --delegate-file /scratch/delegate.json reader investigate incident 4471
send-agent --tag req3 --delegate-file /scratch/delegate.json reader investigate incident 4471
